=== REASONING ===
Chosen approach (real infrastructure, deterministic, no real network/auth — mirrors the shipped
-uiTestLiveDemo / -uiTestPushDemo pattern):
  1. A launch-argument harness (Sources/Testing/UITestConfig.swift) parsed once; inert in the
     shipping app (no flags => no behaviour change). Drives a component gallery, a leaf-contract
     page-state harness, a deterministic initial route, appearance + Dynamic Type overrides.
  2. ComponentGalleryView — every shared TS* category in its states, each element with a stable
     accessibilityIdentifier and interactive controls that echo their state (retry counter, search echo).
  3. PageStateHarnessView — the P4 leaf-contract states (loading/empty/error+retry/success/stale/
     offline) built from the SAME shared chrome the 153 units compose, with a working error→success
     retry and a connectivity launch arg that lands directly on stale/offline.
  4. Additive accessibility identifiers on the REAL shell (AppShell sidebar/tabs/More/command-palette/
     RouteHost) + TSCommandPalette, so the suites drive the real navigation, not a fake screen.
  5. Six idiom-aware XCUITest suites (Tests/UI) covering components, page states, navigation idioms,
     deep links, and accessibility/appearance.

Rejected alternatives (and why):
  * One bespoke harness per 153 units (765 state permutations): impractical, fragile against 153
     distinct InMemory-source APIs, and duplicates the per-unit logic already unit-tested by each
     co-located *.Tests.swift. Replaced by a real shared-chrome state harness + real-shell coverage.
  * Overriding accessibilityReduceMotion via .environment: the keypath is read-only in Swift 6
     (`KeyPath & Sendable`, not WritableKeyPath) — cannot be set at the UI-test boundary. Appearance
     + Dynamic Type ARE driven (real modifiers); Reduce-Motion branch logic stays unit-tested (P9-0001
     scope) and the motion components are still exercised for rendering/accessibility.
  * Changing macOS signing/entitlements to dodge the dev-cert requirement: out of scope — it would
     alter the shipping app's security posture and the P99 acceptance gate. Left as a capability block.
  * Fixing the 67 pre-existing placeholder false-positives and the 14 predecessor unit-test compile
     errors: out-of-scope churn across dozens of predecessor files that would not change the BLOCKED
     outcome (macOS signing is unfixable here). Recorded, not silently "fixed".

